==Strategy==
Obviously, with there being a hoard of Metal Enemies, bringing units that do things against Metals works well. Whether they can Crit, like with [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]], [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], etc. or do something else against them, like [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoop Cat]], [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Clockwork Cat]], [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Drumcorps Cat]], [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Primordial Cat]], etc. will make the Metals easier to handle. [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] could work, the only issue lies in the fact that there are a decent amount of Metal Doges in this stage to make it that she may hit one of them instead of the bigger threats, like Sir Metal Seal.

That's only half of it. The other part is taking out Gilgamesh, since his massive range (and blindspot) will do lots of damage over time. Since he has a Blindspot, Rushers like [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], even [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]] can do wonders at keeping him back. Just make sure they don't get halted by other Metal Enemies.

